hadiths[126]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23324","Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, al-Husayn informed us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to us, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting on Hira, and with him were Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them, and the mountain shook, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Be firm, Hira, for there is upon you none but a Prophet, or a Siddiq, or a martyr."
"23325","Ali ibn al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Shaqiq, narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to us, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The covenant between us and them is prayer, so whoever abandons it has disbelieved."
"23326","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Zuhayr narrated to us, from Wasil ibn Hibban al-Bajali, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying, he said: Truffle is a cure for the eye, and Ajwa is of the fruit of Paradise, and this black seed, Ibn Burayda said, meaning al-Shuniz which is in salt, is a cure from every disease except death."
"23327","Affan narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to me, my father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not say to the hypocrite: Our master, for if he is your master, you have angered your Lord, Almighty."
"23328","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Sinan narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows, of them eighty are from this umma. And Affan once said: You are of them eighty rows."
"23329","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to us, he said: I and my father entered upon Mu'awiya, so he seated us on carpets, then we were brought food and we ate, then we were brought drink, so Mu'awiya drank, then he handed to my father, then he said: I have not drunk it since the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade it. Mu'awiya said: I was the most handsome of the youth of Quraysh and the best of them in teeth, and there was nothing I found delight in as I found when young except milk, or a man of good speech talking to me."
"23330","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bashir ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a man called Ma'iz ibn Malik came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have committed adultery and I want you to purify me. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Return. Then when it was the next day, he came to him also and confessed to him adultery, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him: Return. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to his people and asked them about him, so he said to them: What do you know of Ma'iz ibn Malik al-Aslami, do you see any harm in him or deny anything of his mind. They said: O Prophet of Allah, we see no harm in him and we deny nothing of his mind. Then he returned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a third time and confessed to him adultery also, so he said: O Prophet of Allah, purify me. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent to his people also and asked them about him, so they said to him as they said to him the first time: We see no harm in him and we deny nothing of his mind. Then he returned to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, a fourth time also and confessed to him adultery, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered, and we dug for him a pit, and he was placed in it to his chest, then he ordered the people to stone him. And Burayda said: We, the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to talk among ourselves that Ma'iz ibn Malik, had he sat in his baggage after his confession three times, he would not have been sought, and he only stoned him at the fourth."
"23331","al-Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Abu Isra'il informed us, from Harith ibn Hasira, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: He entered upon Mu'awiya, and a man was speaking, so Burayda said: O Mu'awiya, permit me to speak. He said: Yes, while he thought he would speak like what the other said. So Burayda said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I hope to intercede on the Day of Resurrection the number of what is on earth of tree and clod. He said: Do you hope it yourself, O Mu'awiya, while Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, does not hope it."
"23332","al-Khuza'i, and he is Abu Salama, narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Bakr ibn Ahmar, his name is Jibril, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: A man of Azd died and left no heir, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Seek for him an heir, seek for him a relative. He said: None was found, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Hand it to the eldest of Khuza'a."
"23333","al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, Ibn Abi Ghaniyya narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Burayda, he said: I raided with Ali in Yemen, and I saw from him harshness, then when I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I mentioned Ali and belittled him, so I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, change, so he said: O Burayda, am I not more worthy of the believers than themselves. I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Whomever I am his mawla, then Ali is his mawla."
"23334","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did not take evil omens from anything, but when he wanted to approach a woman, he asked about her name, then if it was good, joy was seen in his face, and if it was ugly, that was seen in his face. And when he sent a man, he asked about his name, then if it was a good name, joy was seen in his face, and if it was ugly, that was seen in his face."
"23335","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bashir narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: I was sent, I and the Hour together; it almost preceded me."
"23336","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bashir narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us one day and called three times, so he said: O people, do you know what is my likeness and your likeness. They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: My likeness and your likeness is but the likeness of a people who feared an enemy coming to them, so they sent a man to scout for them, then while they were thus, he saw the enemy, so he came to warn them, and he feared the enemy would catch him before he warned his people, so he waved with his garment: O people, you are attacked, O people, you are attacked, three times."
"23337","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bashir narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a woman of Ghamid came to him and said: O Prophet of Allah, I have committed adultery and I want you to purify me. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Return. Then when it was the next day, she came to him also and confessed to him adultery, so she said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery and I want you to purify me. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Return. Then when it was the next day, she came to him also and confessed to him adultery, so she said: O Prophet of Allah, purify me, perhaps you will turn me away as you turned away Ma'iz ibn Malik, for by Allah I am pregnant. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: Return until you give birth. Then when she gave birth, she came with the boy carrying him, and said: O Prophet of Allah, this, I have given birth. He said: Then go and nurse him until you wean him. Then when she weaned him, she came with the boy, in his hand a piece of bread, she said: O Prophet of Allah, this, I have weaned him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered for the boy and handed him to a man of the Muslims, and ordered for her, so a pit was dug for her, and she was placed in it to her chest, then he ordered the people to stone her. Then Khalid ibn al-Walid came with a stone and threw her head, so blood spattered on the cheek of Khalid, and he reviled her. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard his reviling her, so he said: Gently, O Khalid ibn al-Walid, do not revile her, for by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, she has repented a repentance, had the collector of taxes repented it, he would have been forgiven. So he ordered for her, and prayer was said over her, and she was buried."
"23338","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bashir ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard him say: Learn Surat al-Baqara, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the magicians cannot bear it. He said: Then he waited a while, then he said: Learn Surat al-Baqara and Al Imran, for they are the two bright ones, shading their companion on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks. And the Qur'an will meet its companion on the Day of Resurrection when his grave splits from him, like a pale man, so he says to him: Do you know me. So he says: I do not know you. So he says to him: Do you know me. So he says: I do not know you. So he says: I am your companion, the Qur'an, who made you thirst in the midday heats and kept your night awake. And every trader is behind his trade, and you today are behind every trade. So he will be given kingship in his right and eternity in his left, and a crown of dignity will be placed on his head, and his parents will be clothed with two garments the people of the world cannot value, so they say: For what were we clothed this. So it will be said: For your child's taking the Qur'an. Then it will be said to him: Recite and ascend in the degrees of Paradise and its chambers, so he will be in ascent as long as he recites, whether fast or measured."
"23339","Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Bashir ibn Muhajir narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: I was sitting with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: My umma will be driven by a people broad of faces, small of eyes, as if their faces are shields, three times, until they join them to the Arabian Peninsula. As for the first wave, whoever flees of them will be saved. And as for the second, some will perish and some will be saved. And as for the third, all who remain of them will be afflicted. They said: O Prophet of Allah, who are they. He said: They are the Turks. He said: Nay, by Him in Whose Hand is my soul, they will tie their horses to the pillars of the mosques of the Muslims. He said: And Burayda would not part from two or three camels, and travel goods and waterskins after that, to flee from what he heard from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of the tribulation from the rulers of the Turks."
"23340","Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Malik informed us, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: Burayda went out in the evening, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met him, so he took his hand and took him into the mosque, and there was the voice of a man reciting. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you see him showing off. So Burayda fell silent. And there was a man supplicating, so he said: O Allah, I ask You by my bearing witness that You are Allah, Whom there is no god but You, the One, the Eternal, Who did not beget and was not begotten, and there is none like unto Him. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, he has asked Allah by His Greatest Name, which when asked by He gives, and when supplicated by He answers. He said: Then when it was the next year, Burayda went out in the evening, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, met him, so he took his hand and took him into the mosque, and there was the voice of the man reciting. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you say he is showing off. So Burayda said: Do you say he is showing off, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No, rather a believing penitent, no, rather a believing penitent. And there was al-Ash'ari reciting with a voice of his in the side of the mosque. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Al-Ash'ari, or Abd Allah ibn Qays, was given a flute from the flutes of Dawud. So I said: Shall I not inform him, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes, inform him. So I informed him, so he said: You are to me a friend, you informed me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, of a hadith."
"23341","Yazid narrated to us, al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, that his father raided with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sixteen raids."
"23342","Mu'tamir narrated to us, from Kahmas, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: He raided with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sixteen raids."
"23343","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and asked him about the time of prayer, so he said: Pray with us these two. So he ordered Bilal when the dawn rose, and he called the adhan, then he ordered him and he established, then he ordered him and he called the adhan when the sun declined, for Zuhr, then he ordered him and he established, then he ordered him and he established Asr while the sun was high, then he ordered him and he established Maghrib when the edge of the sun disappeared, then he ordered him when the twilight disappeared and he established Isha, and he prayed. Then he ordered him the next day and he established Fajr, and he brightened with it, then he ordered him and he cooled Zuhr, and he was gracious in cooling it, then he prayed Asr while the sun was white, delaying it beyond what he had done, and he established Maghrib before the twilight disappeared, then he ordered him and he established Isha when a third of the night had gone, then he said: Where is the asker about the time of prayer. The man said: I, O Messenger of Allah. So he said: The time of your prayers is between what you saw."
"23344","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Abd Allah ibn Ata al-Makki, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, that a woman came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave charity to my mother with a slave girl, then she died, and she returned to me in inheritance. He said: Allah has rewarded you and returned to you in inheritance. She said: My mother died and did not perform hajj, will it suffice her if I perform hajj for her. He said: Yes. She said: My mother owed the fast of a month, will it suffice her if I fast for her. He said: Yes."
"23345","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham al-Dastuwai informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Malih, he said: We were with Burayda in an expedition on a cloudy day, so he said: Pray early, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever abandons the Asr prayer, his deed is frustrated."
"23346","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Dirar, meaning Ibn Murra Abu Sinan, narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them. And I forbade you from the meats of sacrifices to keep them beyond three, so keep them as seems to you. And I forbade you from nabidh except in a waterskin, so drink in all vessels, and do not drink intoxicant."
"23347","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Malih, from Burayda, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever abandons the Asr prayer, his deed is frustrated."
"23348","Ismail narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, from Abd Allah ibn Mawala, he said: While I was traveling in al-Ahwaz, I was with a man walking before me on a mule or she-mule, and he was saying: O Allah, the generation of this umma is gone, so join me with them. So I said: And me, so include me in your supplication. He said: And this companion of mine, if he wants that. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best of my umma is my generation of them, then those who follow them. He said: And I do not know whether he mentioned the third or not. Then peoples will succeed in whom fatness appears, pouring out testimony without being asked. He said: And he was Burayda al-Aslami."
"23349","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Ubayda, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent us in a sariyya. He said: When we came, he said: How did you see the companionship of your companion. He said: So I complained of him, or another complained of him. He said: So I raised my head, and I was a bent man. He said: And the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, his face had reddened. He said: While he says: Whomever I am his wali, then Ali is his wali."
"23350","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: Abu Mu'awiya said, and I do not think he heard it from him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No man brings out anything of charity until he frees it from the jaws of seventy devils."
"23351","Ismail narrated to us, Uyayna ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Burayda al-Aslami, he said: I went out one day for a need, and I was with the Prophet, upon him prayer and peace, walking before me, so he took my hand and we went walking together, and there before us was a man praying, increasing bowing and prostration. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you see him showing off. So I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. So he left my hand from his hand, then joined his hands, making them point and raising them, and saying: Upon you a moderate course, upon you a moderate course, upon you a moderate course, for whoever contends with this religion, it will overcome him."
"23352","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: The believer dies with sweat of the forehead."
"23353","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard a man say: O Allah, I ask You by my bearing witness that You are Allah, Whom there is no god but You, the One, the Eternal, Who did not beget and was not begotten, and there is none like unto Him. So he said: He has asked Allah by the Greatest Name of Allah, which when asked by He gives, and when supplicated by He answers."
"23354","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sufyan, Alqama ibn Marthad narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed the prayers with one wudu on the day of the Conquest. So Umar said to him: You have done something you did not do. He said: Deliberately I did it."
"23355","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd al-Jalil narrated to us, he said: I came to a circle in which were Abu Mijlaz and Ibn Burayda, so Abd Allah ibn Burayda said: My father Burayda narrated to me, he said: I hated Ali with a hatred none ever hated, he said: And I loved a man of Quraysh, I did not love him except for his hatred of Ali. He said: So that man was sent over cavalry, so I accompanied him, I did not accompany him except for his hatred of Ali. He said: So we took captives. He said: So he wrote to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Send to us one to take the fifth. He said: So he sent to us Ali, and among the captives was a slave girl, the best of the captives, so he took the fifth and divided, then his head came out covered. So we said: O Abu al-Hasan, what is this. He said: Did you not see the slave girl among the captives, for I divided and took the fifth, so she fell in the fifth, then she fell in the household of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then she fell in the family of Ali, and I had intercourse with her. He said: So the man wrote to the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so I said: Send me, so he sent me as a confirmer. He said: So I read the letter saying: He spoke truth. He said: So he held my hand and the letter and said: Do you hate Ali. He said: I said: Yes. He said: Then do not hate him, and if you loved him, increase for him in love, for by Him in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, the share of the family of Ali in the fifth is better than a slave girl. He said: So there was none of the people after the saying of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, more beloved to me than Ali. Abd Allah said: By Him besides Whom there is no god, there is none between me and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in this hadith but my father Burayda."
"23356","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Sharik, Abu Rabi'a narrated to us, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah, Almighty, loves of my companions four; He told me He loves them and commanded me to love them. They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Ali is of them, and Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, and Salman al-Farisi, and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad al-Kindi."
"23357","Malik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Abd Allah ibn Qays al-Ash'ari was given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"23358","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, al-A'mash informed us, from Abu Dawud, from Burayda, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, for him every day is charity, and whoever grants him respite after it is due, for him the like of it every day is charity."
"23359","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: A woman came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: I gave charity to my mother with a slave girl, and she died. He said: Allah has rewarded you and returned to you the inheritance."
"23360","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Salih, meaning Ibn Hayyan, narrated to us, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, that he was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among forty-two of his companions, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was praying in the Maqam, and they were behind him sitting waiting for him. Then when he prayed, he leaned between him and the Ka'ba as if he wanted to take something, then he turned to his companions, and they rose, and he gestured to them with his hand to sit, so they sat. So he said: You saw me when I finished my prayer, I leaned between me and the Ka'ba as if I wanted to take something. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Paradise was displayed to me, and I never saw the like of what is in it. And a cluster of grapes passed by me and pleased me, so I leaned to it to take it, but it preceded me. And had I taken it, I would have planted it among you until you ate of the fruit of Paradise. And know that truffle is a cure for the eye, and Ajwa is of the fruit of Paradise, and this black seed which is in salt, know that it is a cure from every disease except death."
"23361","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when it was the day of the Conquest, the conquest of Makka, performed wudu and wiped over his khuffs. So Umar said to him: I saw you, O Messenger of Allah, do today something you did not do. He said: Deliberately I did it, O Umar."
"23362","Waki' narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Rabi'a, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not follow the glance with the glance, for you have the first, and you do not have the other."
"23363","Waki' narrated to us, Bashir ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Learn al-Baqara, for taking it is blessing and leaving it is regret, and the magicians cannot bear it. Learn al-Baqara and Al Imran, for they are the two bright ones, coming on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or as if they were two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading for their companion."
"23364","Waki' narrated to us, Bashir ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Qur'an will come on the Day of Resurrection like a pale man, so it will say to its companion: I am who kept your night awake and made your midday heats thirsty."
"23365","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sanctity of the wives of the mujahidin for those who sit is like the sanctity of their mothers. And there is no man of those who sit who succeeds a man of the mujahidin in his family and betrays him in her, but he will be stood for him on the Day of Resurrection, so he will take from his deed what he wills. So what do you think."
"23366","Waki' narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he sent a commander over a sariyya or army, advised him in his own self to fear Allah, and those with him of the Muslims with good, and said: Invade in the name of Allah, in the way of Allah, fight whoever disbelieves in Allah. So when you meet your enemy of the polytheists, call them to one of three traits or qualities, so whichever of them they answer you to, accept from them and refrain from them. Call them to Islam, then if they answer you, accept from them, then call them to move from their abode to the abode of the Muhajirin, and inform them if they do that, that for them is what is for the Muhajirin, and upon them is what is upon the Muhajirin. Then if they refuse and choose their abode, inform them that they will be like the Bedouin Muslims, the ruling of Allah which applies to the believers applies to them, and they will have no share in fay and booty except to strive with the Muslims. Then if they refuse, call them to give the jizya, then if they answer, accept from them and refrain from them. Then if they refuse, seek help from Allah, then fight them."
"23367","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever plays with nardashir, it is as if he dipped his hand in the flesh of a pig and its blood. And Waki' once did not attribute it."
"23368","Waki' narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Tha'laba al-Tai narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He is not of us who swears by amanah, and whoever corrupts a wife against her husband, or a slave against his master, is not of us."
"23369","Waki' narrated to us, Dalham ibn Salih narrated to us, from a shaykh called Hujayr ibn Abd Allah al-Kindi, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, that al-Najashi gifted to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, two black plain khuffs, so he wore them, then performed wudu and wiped over them."
"23370","Yazid narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: A man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love horses, so are there horses in Paradise. He said: If Allah admits you to Paradise, you will not wish to ride a horse of red ruby flying with you wherever you wish in Paradise but you will ride. And another man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, are there camels in Paradise. He said: O servant of Allah, if Allah admits you to Paradise, you will have therein what your soul desires and your eye delights in."
"23371","Abu Ubayda al-Haddad narrated to us, Thawwab ibn Utba narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Fitr would not go out until he ate, and on the day of Nahr would not eat until he returned."
"23372","Yunus narrated to us, Uqba ibn Abd Allah al-Rifa'i narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would not go in the morning on the day of Fitr until he ate, and would not eat on the day of Adha until he returned, then ate of his sacrifice."
"23373","Mu'awiya ibn Hisham and Abu Ahmad narrated to us, they said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught them when they went out to the graves, so their speaker would say: Peace upon you, people of the abodes, of the believers and Muslims. Mu'awiya said in his hadith: We, God willing, will join you; you are our predecessors and we are for you followers; and we ask Allah for us and for you well-being."
"23374","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Abd Allah narrated to me, he said: I heard my father Burayda say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Five none knows but Allah, the Exalted: Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and knows what is in the wombs, and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in which land it will die. Allah is Knowing, Aware."
"23375","Zayd, and he is Ibn al-Hubab, narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: Jibril, peace upon him, was withheld from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, so he said to him: What withheld you. He said: We do not enter a house in which is a dog."
"23376","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ismail informed us, from Abu Dawud al-A'ma, from Burayda al-Khuza'i, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, we knew how to greet you, so how do we pray upon you. He said: Say: O Allah, make Your prayers, mercy, and blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You made them upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim. You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"23377","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, that a black slave girl came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he returned from one of his raids, and said: I vowed, if Allah returned you righteous, to beat the duff before you. He said: If you did, then do, and if you did not, then do not do. So she beat, then Abu Bakr entered while she beat, and others entered while she beat, then Umar entered. He said: So she put her duff behind her, while veiled. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Satan flees from you, O Umar. I am sitting here, and these entered, then when you entered, she did what she did."
"23378","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The lineages of the people of the world they go to is this wealth."
"23379","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Rabi'a, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said to Ali: O Ali, do not follow the glance with the glance, for you have the first, and you do not have the other."
"23380","Zayd, and he is Ibn al-Hubab, narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, he said: I heard my father Burayda say: While the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was walking, a man came with a donkey and said: O Messenger of Allah, ride. So the man stepped back. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No, you are more entitled to the front of your mount than me, unless you give it to me. He said: I have given it to you. He said: So he rode."
"23381","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, my father Burayda narrated to me, he said: We besieged Khaybar, so Abu Bakr took the banner and returned without conquest for him. Then he took it the next day and went out and returned without conquest for him, and the people suffered that day hardship and strain. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I will hand the banner tomorrow to a man whom Allah and His Messenger love, and who loves Allah and His Messenger; he will not return until conquest is for him. So we spent the night with our souls pleased that conquest is tomorrow. Then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke, he prayed the morning prayer, then stood standing and called for the banner, and the people were on their ranks. So he called Ali, while he had sore eyes, and spat in his eyes, and handed to him the banner, and conquest was for him. Burayda said: And I am of those who craned for it."
"23382","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, recited in the Isha prayer by Wash-Shamsi wa Duhaha and the like of it of suras."
"23383","Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, he said: I heard my father Burayda say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was addressing us, then al-Hasan and al-Husayn came, upon them two red shirts, walking and stumbling. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended from the minbar and carried them and placed them before him, then said: Allah and His Messenger spoke truth: Your wealth and children are but a trial. I looked at these two boys walking and stumbling, and I could not bear until I cut my speech and lifted them."
"23384","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda informed me, he said: I heard my father Burayda say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, awoke and called Bilal, so he said: O Bilal, with what did you precede me to Paradise. I never entered Paradise but I heard your movement before me. Last night I entered Paradise and heard your movement, then I came to a palace of gold, high and lofty. So I said: Whose is this palace. They said: For a man of the Arabs. I said: I am an Arab; whose is this palace. They said: For a man of the Muslims, of the umma of Muhammad. I said: I am Muhammad; whose is this palace. They said: For Umar ibn al-Khattab. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Were it not for your jealousy, O Umar, I would have entered the palace. So he said: O Messenger of Allah, would I be jealous toward you. He said: And he said to Bilal: With what did you precede me to Paradise. He said: I never innovated hadath but I performed wudu and prayed two rak'as. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: By this."
"23385","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, he said: I heard Burayda say: Salman came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he arrived in Madina, with a table upon it ripe dates, and placed it before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is this, O Salman. He said: Charity upon you and upon your companions. He said: Lift it, for we do not eat charity. So he lifted it. Then he came the next day with the like of it and placed it before him, carrying it. So he said: What is this, O Salman. So he said: A gift for you. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his companions: Spread. Then he looked at the seal on the back of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and believed in him. And he belonged to the Jews, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bought him for so many dirhams, and on planting palms, Salman working in them until they bear. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, planted the palms except one palm Umar planted, so the palms bore that year, and the palm did not bear. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is the matter with this. Umar said: I planted it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pulled it, then planted it, and it bore that year."
"23386","Zayd narrated to us, Husayn narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, he said: I heard my father Burayda say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: In man are three hundred and sixty joints, so upon him to give charity for every joint of them a charity. They said: Who can bear that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Spittle in the mosque you bury it, or a thing you remove from the road. Then if you cannot, the two rak'as of Duha suffice you."
"23387","Zayd narrated to us, Husayn narrated to me, Abd Allah narrated to me, he said: I heard my father Burayda say: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Upon you is the black seed, and it is al-Shuniz, for in it is healing."
"23388","Bakr ibn Isa narrated to us, Abu Awana narrated to us, Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to us, from Abu Zuhayr, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Spending in Hajj is like spending in the way of Allah, seven hundred fold."
"23389","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, he said: I heard my father say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, performed aqiqa for al-Hasan and al-Husayn."
"23390","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Dirar, meaning Ibn Murra Abu Sinan al-Shaybani, narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; this umma of that is eighty rows. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Bishr ibn al-Harith, Abu al-Ahwas, and al-Haytham ibn Kharija died in the year two hundred and twenty-seven."
"23391","Hasan ibn Musa and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, they said: Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik said in his hadith: Zubayd ibn al-Harith al-Yami narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: We were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he alighted with us, and we with him were near a thousand riders, so he prayed two rak'as, then turned to us with his face, and his eyes were shedding tears. So Umar ibn al-Khattab stood to him, ransoming him with father and mother, saying: O Messenger of Allah, what is with you. He said: I asked my Lord, Almighty, for forgiveness for my mother, and He did not permit me, so my eyes wept mercy for her from the Fire. And I forbade you three: from visiting graves, so visit them, that your visiting them remind you good. And I forbade you from the meats of sacrifices after three, so eat and keep what you wish. And I forbade you from drinks in vessels, so drink in any vessel you wish, and do not drink intoxicant."
"23392","Abu Mu'awiya narrated to us, from Layth, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The excellence of the wives of the mujahidin over those who sit, in sanctity, is like the excellence of their mothers. And there is no sitter who succeeds a mujahid in his family and corrupts his family, but he will be stood for him on the Day of Resurrection. It will be said to him: This betrayed you in your family, so take from his deed what you wish. He said: So what do you think."
"23393","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I forbade you from visiting graves, so visit them, for it reminds the Hereafter. And I forbade you from nabidh of the jar, so make nabidh in every vessel, and avoid every intoxicant. And I forbade you from eating the meats of sacrifices after three, so eat, provision, and store."
"23394","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, from his book, Husayn narrated to me, Ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever swears he is free from Islam, then if he is lying, he is as he said, and if he is truthful, he will not return to Islam sound."
"23395","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Between us and them is abandonment of prayer, so whoever abandons it has disbelieved."
"23396","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to us, he said: I heard my father Burayda say: Mu'adh ibn Jabal, he says, led his companions in Isha prayer and recited in it Iqtarabat al-Sa'a, so a man stood before he finished and prayed and went. So Mu'adh said to him a harsh word. So the man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and excused himself to him, so he said: I worked in palms and feared for the water. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Pray by Wash-Shamsi wa Duhaha and the like of it of suras."
"23397","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to me, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, handed the banner to Ali ibn Abi Talib on the day of Khaybar."
"23398","Yahya ibn Wadih Abu Tumayla narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid informed me, he said: I heard Ibn Burayda say: I heard my father say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Whoever says I am free from Islam, then if he is lying, he is as he said, and if he is truthful, he will not return to Islam."
"23399","Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us, Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrated to me, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, returned from one of his raids, and a black slave girl came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed, if Allah returned you safe, to beat the duff over your head. So he said: If you vowed, then do, else not. She said: I vowed. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sat, and she beat the duff."
"23400","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Ajlah al-Kindi narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father Burayda, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent two expeditions to Yemen, over one of them Ali ibn Abi Talib, and over the other Khalid ibn al-Walid. So he said: When you meet, Ali is over the people, and if you separate, each of you is over his army. He said: So we met Banu Zayd of the people of Yemen and we fought, so the Muslims overcame the polytheists, so we killed the fighters and enslaved the offspring. So Ali chose a woman of the captives for himself. Burayda said: So Khalid ibn al-Walid wrote with me to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informing him of that. Then when I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I handed the letter, so it was read to him, and I saw anger in the face of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the place of the seeker of refuge; you sent me with a man and commanded me to obey him, so I did what I was sent with. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not fall upon Ali, for he is from me and I am from him, and he is your wali after me. And he is from me and I am from him, and he is your wali after me."
"23401","Khalid ibn al-Walid, may Allah be pleased with him, having seen this, wrote a letter to the service of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informing him of it, and he gave that letter to me to deliver it; I came into the Prophetic presence and presented the letter, and the letter was read out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I saw signs of anger on the luminous face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); I said: O Messenger of Allah, I seek refuge with Allah; you sent me with a man and commanded me to obey him, and I acted upon that instruction; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not fall into any misconception concerning Ali; he is from me and I am from him, and he is your beloved after me; he said this sentence twice."
"23402","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Abu Rabiah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to love four of my Companions; Sharik, I think, said: And he informed me that He loves them: Ali is among them, and Abu Dharr, and Salman, and al-Miqdad al-Kindi."
"23403","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, that he narrated from Abdillah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from his father Buraydah ibn Husayb, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves, so visit them, for in visiting them is admonition and lesson; and I had forbidden you the meat of sacrifices beyond three days, so eat and store; and I had forbidden you nabidh in these skins, so drink, but do not drink what is unlawful."
"23404","Muammal narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves, and the meat of sacrifices to be kept beyond three days, and vessels; and I had forbidden you the meat of sacrifices so that the one of means may make room for the one who has no means, so eat and store; and I had forbidden you visiting graves, and indeed Muhammad has been permitted to visit his mother's grave; and I had forbidden you vessels, and indeed vessels neither forbid anything nor permit it; and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"23405","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Jabir narrated to us, from Simak, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: I went out with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when we were at Waddan, he said: Stay in your places until I come to you; so he went forth, then he came to us while he was unwell, and said: I came to the grave of Muhammad's mother, and I asked my Lord for intercession, but He denied it to me; and I had forbidden you visiting graves, so visit them; and I had forbidden you the meat of sacrifices after three days, so eat and keep what seems good to you; and I had forbidden you these drinks in these vessels, so drink in whatever seems good to you."
"23406","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya of the people of Merv narrated to us, Aws ibn Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, he said: My brother Sahl ibn Abdillah ibn Buraydah informed me, from his father, from his grandfather Buraydah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be many expeditions after me, so be in the expedition of Khurasan, then settle in the city of Merv, for Dhu al-Qarnayn built it and supplicated for blessing for it, and no evil will harm its people."
"23407","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Ubaydillah al-Ataki, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is a duty; whoever does not perform witr is not of us; he said it three times."
"23408","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Layth, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To them belongs what they accepted Islam upon of their lands, their slaves, and their livestock, and upon them concerning it is nothing except charity."
"23409","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq and Abu Rabiah al-Iyadi, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: O Ali, do not follow one glance with another glance, for only the first is for you, and the latter is not for you."
"23410","Bahz narrated to us, Muthanna ibn Said narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, that he was in Khurasan and visited a brother of his who was sick, and found him dying, and his forehead sweating, so he said: Allah is Greatest; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The death of the believer is with sweat of the forehead."
"23411","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih al-Azdi narrated to us with the doubled tha, Khalid ibn Ubayd Abu Isam informed me, Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me to a place in the desert near Makkah, and it was dry land around which was sand, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Beast will emerge from this place, and it will be a handspan within a span."
"23412","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abdillah ibn Mawalah, he said: I was traveling with Buraydah al-Aslami, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The best of this ummah are the generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then there will be a people whose testimony precedes their oaths and whose oaths precede their testimony; and Affan once said: The generation among whom I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then those who follow them."
"23413","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever plays with nardashir, it is as if he dips his hands in the flesh of swine and its blood."
"23414","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, that Abu al-Malih narrated to him, he said: We were with Buraydah on a campaign on a cloudy day, and he said: Offer prayer early, for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons Asr prayer, his deed has come to naught."
"23415","Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abu Fulanah informed us, thus said my father, he did not name him deliberately, and another narrated it to us and named him, meaning Abu Hanifah, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man who came to him: Go, for the one who guides to good is like its doer."
"23416","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, that he passed by a gathering while they were disparaging Ali, so he stood over them and said: There had been something in myself against Ali, and Khalid ibn al-Walid was likewise; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me in a detachment under Ali's command, and we captured captives; Ali took a slave girl from the khumus for himself; Khalid ibn al-Walid said: Here you are; when we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I began telling him what had happened, then I said: Ali took a slave girl from the khumus; and I was a forthright man; so I raised my head, and the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had changed, and he said: Of whomever I am his wali, Ali is his wali."
"23417","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution at every prayer, but on the day of the Conquest he performed ablution, wiped over his khuffs, and prayed the prayers with one ablution; Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you did something you did not use to do; he said: I did it deliberately, O Umar."
"23418","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a commander over an army or a detachment, he enjoined him in his own affair to fear Allah, and those with him of the Muslims with good, then he said: Go forth in the name of Allah, in the way of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah; go forth, do not misappropriate spoils, do not betray, do not mutilate, and do not kill a child; and when you meet your enemy of the polytheists, call them to one of three qualities, and whichever of them they answer you to, accept from them and refrain from them; then call them to move from their abode to the abode of the Muhajirun, and inform them that if they do so, for them is what is for the Muhajirun and upon them is what is upon the Muhajirun; and if they refuse to move from it, inform them that they will be like the Bedouin Muslims, the ruling of Allah which applies to the Muslims applies to them, and they will have nothing in booty and fay except that they strive with the Muslims; and if they refuse, ask them for jizyah, and if they answer you, accept from them and refrain from them; and if they refuse, seek help from Allah and fight them; and when you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to grant them Allah's covenant and His Prophet's covenant, do not grant them Allah's covenant nor His Prophet's covenant, but grant them your covenant and your father's covenant and your companions' covenants, for your breaking your covenants and your fathers' covenants is lighter than breaking Allah's covenant and His Messenger's covenant; and if you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to bring them down upon Allah's judgment, do not bring them down upon Allah's judgment, but bring them down upon your judgment, for you do not know whether you will hit Allah's judgment concerning them or not; Abd al-Rahman said: This or the like of it."
"23419","Muhammad ibn Jafar and Rawh, the meaning, said: Awf narrated to us, from Maymun Abu Abdillah, Rawh said al-Kurdi, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father Buraydah al-Aslami, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) encamped at the fortress of Khaybar's people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the banner to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and those who rose of the Muslims rose with him, and they met Khaybar's people; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall surely give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love; on the morrow he called Ali while he had ophthalmia, spat in his eyes, gave him the banner, and the people rose with him; he met Khaybar's people, and Marhab was chanting before them, saying: Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, armed, a tried hero; I thrust at times and at times I strike, when lions come raging; he and Ali exchanged two blows, and he struck him on his head until the sword reached his molars with it, and the people of the camp heard the sound of his blow; and the last of the people had not yet caught up with Ali before victory was granted to him and to them."
"23420","Ibn Numayr narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Ata narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I gave a slave girl as charity to my mother, then my mother died and the slave girl remained; he said: Your reward has become due, and she has returned to you in inheritance; she said: My mother owed fasting a month, shall I fast on her behalf; he said: Yes; she said: My mother did not perform Hajj, shall I perform Hajj on her behalf; he said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your mother."
"23421","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, Malik ibn Mighwal informed me, Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque and took my hand, so I entered with him, and a man was reciting and praying; he said: This one has indeed been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud; and he was Abdillah ibn Qays, Abu Musa al-Ashari; I said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I inform him; he said: So inform him; I informed him, and he said: You have ever been a friend to me."
"23422","Yahya ibn Wadih, and he is Abu Tumaylah, narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Muslim, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a gold ring on a man's hand and said: What is it with you and the ornament of Paradise's people; he came having worn a ring of brass, and he said: I find from you the scent of idol people; he said: Of what shall I make it, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Of silver."
"23423","Rawh narrated to us, Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali to Khalid ibn al-Walid to divide the khumus, and Rawh once said: to take receipt of the khumus; Ali awoke with his head dripping; Khalid said to Buraydah: Do you not see what this one does, because of what Ali did; and I used to hate Ali; then he said: O Buraydah, do you hate Ali; I said: Yes; he said: Do not hate him, Rawh once said: Rather love him, for he has from the khumus more than that."
"23424","Rawh narrated to us, Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali to Khalid ibn al-Walid to divide the khumus, and Rawh once said: to take receipt of the khumus; Ali awoke with his head dripping; Khalid said to Buraydah: Do you not see what this one does, because of what Ali did; and I used to hate Ali; then he said: O Buraydah, do you hate Ali; I said: Yes; he said: Do not hate him, Rawh once said: Rather love him, for he has from the khumus more than that."
"23425","Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In man are three hundred and sixty joints; upon him is to give charity for every joint each day; they said: Who can bear that, O Messenger of Allah; he said: The spittle you see in the mosque and bury it, or a thing you remove from the road; if you cannot, two rakahs of Duha suffice you."
"23426","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Khalaf, meaning Ibn Khalifah, narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided the Conquest campaign and walked out to the graves until when he came to the nearest of them he sat by it as if speaking to a seated person, weeping; Umar ibn al-Khattab met him and said: What makes you weep, may Allah make me your ransom; he said: I asked my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, to permit me to visit the grave of Muhammad's mother, and He permitted me; then I asked Him to permit me to seek forgiveness for her, but He refused; I had forbidden you three things: the meat of sacrifices to keep after three days, so eat what seems good to you; and visiting graves, so whoever wishes let him visit, for I have been permitted to visit the grave of Muhammad's mother, and whoever wishes let him leave; and vessels in which you drink, dubba, hantam, and muzaffat, though I had commanded vessels; and the vessel neither permits anything nor forbids it, so avoid every intoxicant."
"23427","Muhammad ibn Humayd Abu Sufyan narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach them when they went out to the cemeteries to say: Peace be upon you, O people of the abodes, of believers and Muslims; and we, if Allah wills, shall surely join you; you are our forerunners and we are your followers; we ask Allah for us and for you well-being."
"23428","Ali ibn al-Hasan, and he is Ibn Shaqiq, narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, Ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Bilal and said: O Bilal, whereby did you precede me to Paradise; last night I entered Paradise and heard your rustling before me, and I came to a square palace of gold, and said: To whom is this palace; they said: To a man of Muhammad's ummah; I said: I am Muhammad; to whom is this palace; they said: To an Arab man; I said: I am an Arab; to whom is this palace; they said: To a man of Quraysh; I said: I am of Quraysh; to whom is this palace; they said: To Umar ibn al-Khattab; Bilal said: O Messenger of Allah, I never called adhan but I prayed two rakahs, and no minor impurity ever befell me but I performed ablution at it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By this."
"23429","Waki narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man say: O Allah, I ask You by that You are Allah, the One, the Eternal, who did not beget nor was begotten, and there is none like unto Him; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has indeed asked Allah by His Greatest Name, by which if asked He gives, and if supplicated He answers."
"23430","Harami ibn Umarah narrated to us, Thawab ibn Utbah al-Mahri narrated to me, Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when it was Fitir day, would not go out until he ate, and when it was Sacrifice day, would not eat until he sacrificed."
"23431","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Abdillah ibn Mawalah, from Buraydah al-Aslami, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let a servant and a mount suffice one of you of the world."
"23432","Abdillah ibn al-Walid and Muammal said: Sufyan narrated to us, Alqamah ibn Marthad narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that a Bedouin called out in the mosque: Who calls for the red camel, after Fajr; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not find it, may you not find it, may you not find it; these houses, Muammal said: these mosques, were built only for what they were built for."
"23433","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Malih ibn Usamah, from Buraydah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever deliberately abandons Asr prayer, Allah nullifies his deed."
"23434","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, for him for each day is charity like it; then I heard him say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, for him for each day is charity twofold like it; I said: I heard you, O Messenger of Allah, say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, for him for each day is charity like it, then I heard you say: Whoever grants respite to one in hardship, for him for each day is charity twofold like it; he said: For him for each day is charity before the debt falls due; when the debt falls due and he grants him respite, for him for each day is charity twofold like it."
"23435","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn Said, and Abu Dawud, al-Muthanna ibn Said, meaning al-Dubai, narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that he visited a brother of his and saw his forehead sweating, and said: Allah is Greatest; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Abu Dawud said in his hadith: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The believer dies with sweat of the forehead."
"23436","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Hisham, and Ismail, Hisham informed us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu Malih, he said: We were with Buraydah on a campaign on a cloudy day; he said: Offer prayer early, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever abandons Asr prayer, his deed has come to naught."
"23437","Waki narrated to us, Bashir ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn Surah al-Baqarah, for taking it is blessing, abandoning it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot handle it."
"23438","Waki narrated to us, Bashir ibn al-Muhajir narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn al-Baqarah and Al Imran, for they are the two radiant ones; they will come on Resurrection Day as if two clouds, or as if two canopies, or as if two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading for their companion; and Waki once said: disputing on behalf of their companion."
"23439","Waki narrated to us, Said ibn Sinan, and he is Abu Sinan, narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and a man stood and said: Who calls for the red camel; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not find; mosques were built only for what they were built for."
"23440","Waki narrated to us, Abu Janab narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you visiting graves, so visit them, but do not say obscene speech."
"23441","Waki narrated to us, Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Buraydah al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is moderate guidance, for whoever contends harshly with this religion, it will overcome him."
"23442","Waki narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Ata, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I gave a slave girl as charity to my mother, and she died; he said: Allah has rewarded you and returned to you the inheritance."
"23443","Waki narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhajir, from Buraydah, he said: We were with him on a raid; he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Offer prayer early on a cloudy day, for whoever misses Asr prayer, his deed has come to naught."
"23444","Waki and Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Alqamah, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays with nardashir, it is as if he dips his hand in the flesh of swine and its blood."
"23445","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ubaydah, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Of whomever I am his wali, Ali is his wali."
"23446","Ali ibn al-Hasan, and he is Ibn Shaqiq, narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both."
"23447","Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, al-Husayn, he is Ibn Waqid, informed us, Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the objects of pride of this world's people is this wealth."
"23448","Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill and said: Command Abu Bakr to pray with the people; Aishah said: O Messenger of Allah, my father is a tender man; he said: Command Abu Bakr to pray with the people, for you are the companions of Yusuf; so Abu Bakr led the people while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive."
"23449","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim narrated to us, Dirar Abu Sinan narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise's people are one hundred and twenty rows, and this ummah of that is eighty rows."
